 "geometry_notes": [
  "Origin at mid-soffit, y up. Outline built in cm with 48-segment arcs and scaled to mm.",
  "20 cm web = 18 cm web profile with every half-width increased by 1 cm; published area differences are exactly 2 cm x depth for all six types, confirming this.",
  "Bottom flange: printed 15 cm edge (base especial 25), 27 cm to the web; the lower R20 fillet is tangent to the web at 15+27 and its tangent point on the taper is taken at x=22.5 cm (printed 27.5/45/27.5 chord); the taper line is the tangent there and the R5 fillet joins it to the vertical flange edge. The R5 tangent then falls at y=14.8 cm (printed 15).",
  "ESTIMATE: top flange soffit is a straight line from the end of the flange-tip arc, tangent to the upper R20 fillet (which is tangent to the web 32 cm below the top: 10+22). The drawing's break point (x~24.5 cm) is not dimensioned and the catalogue polyline is not tangent; the tangent convention is used.",
  "ESTIMATE: flange tip is a quarter circle R10 from the top corner to the 10 cm edge line (measured from the vector drawing, not printed). Alero especial: 2 cm vertical tip edge, then R8.5 quarter circle (the printed 2 + 8.5 + 2.5 + 20 chain), then the soffit line tangent to R20 (web end 33 cm below top).",
  "ESTIMATE: base especial soffit corners carry a 2 x 2 cm chamfer (drawn, not printed); the other types have square soffit corners as drawn.",
  "Base especial uses the same 45 cm tangent-chord convention although that drawing does not print 45 (drawn tangent ~(22.6, 32.6) cm vs 22.5, 33.1 used)."
 ],
